# Web grounding — cluster tools only (no provider grounding)

Mirrored for Antigravity: [`.agents/rules/web-grounding-cluster-only.md`](../../.agents/rules/web-grounding-cluster-only.md)

## Hard rule

**Do not enable, add, or suggest provider-native web grounding** on LLM requests. That includes opaque upstream search the provider bills and logs outside `ai.log`.

Forbidden in **Gemini / Vertex** request bodies (generateContent, Live setup, etc.):

- `googleSearch`, `enterpriseWebSearch`, `groundingConfig`
- `google_search_retrieval`, `dynamicRetrievalConfig`

Forbidden on **OpenAI / compatible** chat payloads:

- `web_search_options`
- Tools with `"type": "web_search"` or `"web_search_preview"`

This is **final** for Home chat, channels, and Live Call unless the user explicitly asks to **change grounding architecture** (not a one-off model flag).

## What to use instead

| Need | Use |
|------|-----|
| Live facts, news, prices, local listings | **`web.search`** (SearXNG cluster) via tool catalog / Live `web_search` decl |
| Page text | **`web.visit`** |
| Multi-query dossier | **`web.research`** |
| When to search / force hop | **`inst.web_search`** + Rust web pipeline (`prompt-run-test.mdc` **Excluded: web pipeline**) |

Docs: [`_/docs/chat.md`](../../_/docs/chat.md) (Web Grounding), [`_/docs/live-call.md`](../../_/docs/live-call.md) section 4.

## Agent checklist

1. No forbidden keys in Gemini/OpenAI JSON under `servers/**` or `clients/**`.
2. Outgoing Gemini bodies pass `gemini_request_reject_provider_grounding` (`c35_mod_llm`).
3. Before claiming done on LLM/live changes: `.\_\scripts\dev\check_no_provider_grounding.ps1` (or `-Changed`).

## Forbidden vs allowed

```json
// BAD — provider grounding
{ "tools": [{ "googleSearch": {} }] }
```

```json
// GOOD — cluster function tool (name may be web_search on wire)
{ "tools": [{ "functionDeclarations": [{ "name": "web_search", ... }] }] }
```

Prefetch/inject results via `web_grounding_append_user_context` and `tool_loop_run_web_search` — not `groundingConfig`.
